// Two files of one module. The file beside this one wrote `import ledger`, and
// an import binds inside the file that wrote it -- so this file has bound
// nothing and an import written here collides with nothing. What may be
// written here is what an import of its own would reach, and that is one
// question: the answer before the dot and the answer after it agree.
fn main() -> UInt8 {
    ledger.size()
}
